        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "08af9416-b1c4-5bb0-b116-8ae2b1a7f98e",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Richard Wagner, Jules Massenet, Henri Meilhac, Philippe Gille, Abbé Prévost, Emil Scaria\n- Works: Parsifal, Manon, L’histoire du chevalier des Grieux et de Manon Lescaut\n- Places: Bayreuth\n- Roles: Gurnemanz\n\nFacts:\n- In 1731, Abbé Prévost published the novel L’histoire du chevalier des Grieux et de Manon Lescaut.\n- In 1882, Emil Scaria created the role of Gurnemanz in Parsifal for Richard Wagner at Bayreuth.\n- Parsifal, catalogued as WWV 111, is a three-act opera by German composer Richard Wagner.\n- Manon is an opéra comique in five acts by Jules Massenet with a French libretto by Henri Meilhac and Philippe Gille.\n- Manon is based on Abbé Prévost’s 1731 novel L’histoire du chevalier des Grieux et de Manon Lescaut.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
